tle\": \"Director of PCB\" already references PCB. I'll add \"Product Certification Body: Banská Bystrica\" — hmm. Maybe add to address? No. I'll skip it. Actually, could include in issuing_authority as part of name: \"Slovak Legal Metrology (SLM)\" and maybe a \"description\"? Not in schema. Skip.\n\nSignature: Dušan Smigura (page 2) vs Ing. Dušan Šmigura (page 1). person_responsible: \"Ing. Dušan Šmigura, PhD.\" is the fuller form. OK.\n\nWrite final JSON now.\n\nAlso date format: I'll use ISO strings \"2026-09-10\".\n\nOne more: certificate.date_issued — the signature date is 10 September 2026; revision 0 same date. Use 2026-09-10.\n\nLet me make sure numbers: 999999.999 and 999.999999 — decimal conversion from \"999999,999\" and \"999,999999\". Yes: \"999999,999\" → 999999.999 (European decimal comma). And \"999,999999\" → 999.999999. Correct.\n\nScale intervals: 0,001 → 0.001; 0,000001 → 0.000001.\n\nClimatic: −25 (minus sign U+2212 in source) → -25.\n\nOK, compose.",
